.TH TENSOR-GPU-WALLPAPER-SYSTEMD 1 "2026-11-25" "iragonforce/ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
 tensor-gpu-wallpaper-systemd \- guarded Wallpaper Engine systemd supervisor entrypoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tensor-gpu-wallpaper-systemd.py
[--help | --version | --serve]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without --serve the script only prints JSON readiness blockers. --serve is a
future Type=notify systemd user-unit entrypoint that acquires the existing GPU
lease lock and verifies that Hermes, CUDA processes and Ollama models are idle
before spawning the existing wallpaper-engine-sync supervisor. The service
sends READY only after the supervisor process survives a bounded startup wait.
This is not a proof of a rendered wallpaper surface. Restoration grants are not
accepted in this stage. The unit source is NOT installed automatically.
.SH SAFETY
Lease database must be initialized by a future bounded deployment action.
Do not deploy this unit until restoration grant handoff, shutdown semantics,
Hermes integration and rollback are tested on the target machine.
.SH SOURCE
iragonforce/ops, shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-wallpaper-systemd.py
